# Moxa ioThinx 45MR-2606.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioThinx 45MR-2606 — 8-channel DI + 8-channel DO
# | 
# | Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP via ioThinx 4510 adapter, port 502
# | 
# | IMPORTANT: Addresses are MODULE-RELATIVE. Actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address.
# | Slot base depends on which slot this module occupies in the ioThinx 4510 chassis.
# | Only DI ch0-1 support event counter mode; only DO ch0-1 support pulse output mode.
# | 
# | FC01 (coil R/W): doStatus ch0-7 (8 BOOL, 0=OFF 1=ON),
# | diCounterStatus ch0-1 (2 BOOL, 0=Pause 1=Run),
# | diCounterOverflowFlagClear ch0-1 (2 BOOL, W=1 to clear),
# | doPulseStatus ch0-1 (2 BOOL, 0=Stop 1=Start)
# | FC02 (discrete input R): diStatus ch0-7 (8 BOOL, 0=OFF 1=ON),
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioThinx 45MR-2606
@vendor_website=moxa.com
@description=8-DI + 8-DO mixed I/O ioThinx 45MR slot module. Addresses are module-relative; actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address. DI ch0-1 support event counter mode; DO ch0-1 support pulse output mode only. FC01: doStatus ch0-7, diCounterStatus ch0-1, diCounterOverflowFlagClear ch0-1, doPulseStatus ch0-1. FC02: diStatus ch0-7, diMode ch0-7 (0=DI 1=Counter), doMode ch0-7 (0=DO 1=Pulse), diCounterOverflowFlag ch0-1. FC03: diCounterValue ch0-1 u64 (rel 0-7), doStatusAll (rel 8), doPulseCount ch0-1 u64 (rel 9-16), doPulseOnWidth ch0-1 (rel 17-18, unit 500us), doPulseOffWidth ch0-1 (rel 19-20, unit 500us), doPulseStatusAll (rel 21), diCounterStatusAll (rel 22), diCounterOverflowFlagClearAll (rel 23). FC04: diStatusAll, diCounterOverflowFlagAll, diModeAll, doModeAll.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iothinx-45mr-2606.toml; Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
